    "totalDuration": "5 yrs",
    "description": "LegacyJ PERCobol compiles COBOL programs to java. I maintained and enhanced the compiler, which is written in C. I maintained LegacyJ runtime libraries, which ran the compiled java programs. I upgraded our eclipse based IDE to work with the latest version of eclipse. I designed and implemented the VSAM-SQL Bridge, which allows COBOL programs using VSAM  file I/O syntax to access Oracle (or DB2 or any other SQL) databases; this allows companies to port their data from VSAM to Oracle and still use their existing COBOL programs. I designed and implemented the DATACOM-SQL Bridge, which allows COBOL programs written to use CA Datacom verb DBNTRY to access the DATACOM data that has been migrated to SQL. I extended and maintained ISAMJ, which allows COBOL and java programs to access IBM Informix C-ISAM interface and files; C-ISAM is written in C, so ISAMJ translates java requests to C, which it does using JNI (Java Native Interface). I maintained the runtime environment for PERCobol. Setup Oracle 10g. Answered customers’ technical questions and resolved their problems. \nTools: C, Java, EJB, jBoss, XML, JMS, JNDI, java Swing, Servlets, JSP, HTML, JavaScript, JNI, Informix C-ISAM, C, JDBC, SQL, Oracle 10g, Tomcat, Linux, Eclipse (3.2, 3,3, 3,4, and 3.5), COBOL, CICS, DB2, VSAM, CA DATACOM, AS/400 DDS",
